        "Complete real inner-product space H; bounded selfadjoint real operators K,D; I+K²=D²; c≥0 and ‖D‖≤c. Zero H is legal."
      ],
      "statement": "Let H be any complete real inner-product space, including the zero space. Let K,D:H→H be bounded real-linear selfadjoint operators with I+K²=D². Let c≥0 and ‖D‖≤c. Then for every u,v∈H, |(‖u‖²−‖v‖²)/2−⟨Ku,v⟩|≤(c/2)(‖u‖²+‖v‖²). No finite-dimensionality, nontriviality, c≥1, positivity of K or D, or commutation is assumed. This ASTIS auxiliary Hilbert-space lemma supplies the sharp two-component estimate in the PBPS B23 proof; its actual consumer internally produces K,D,c and all hypotheses.",
      "formula": "\\left|\\tfrac12(\\|u\\|^2-\\|v\\|^2)-\\langle Ku,v\\rangle\\right|\\le\\tfrac c2(\\|u\\|^2+\\|v\\|^2).",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Turn the operator square into a norm identity",
          "text": "Evaluate I+K²=D² against x. Selfadjointness moves the outer K and D across the inner product.",
          "formula": "\\|x\\|^2+\\|Kx\\|^2=\\|Dx\\|^2.",
          "lean": "  have hEnergy (x : H) : ‖x‖^2+‖K x‖^2=‖D x‖^2 := by\n    have h := congrArg (fun A : H →L[ℝ] H => inner ℝ (A x) x) hSquare\n    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.add_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.one_apply,\n      ContinuousLinearMap.mul_apply, inner_add_left] at h\n    have hk : inner ℝ (K (K x)) x=inner ℝ (K x) (K x) :=\n      hK.isSymmetric (K x) x\n    have hd : inner ℝ (D (D x)) x=inner ℝ (D x) (D x) :=\n      hD.isSymmetric (D x) x\n    rw [hk, hd] at h\n    simpa only [real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq] using h\n",
